laplacianSchemes
{
  //BW: Depending on the quality of your mesh, blend the fully orthogonal scheme with non-ortho schemes
  //Change value from 0 to 1: 
  //  - 0 is for bad mesh quality, has non-ortho correction, is bounded
  //  - 0.333 for medium-bad mesh quality. Basically the last step because 0 is normally not used.
  //  - 0.5 is medium mesh quality, is less accurate than 1 case, is for non-orthogonal meshes
  //  - 1 is for good mesh quality, has orthogonal correction, is unbounded
    default         Gauss linear limited 0.5;       	
 
/*//BW: For orthogonal meshes with very good quality and uniform cell size
    default         Gauss linear orthogonal;   
*/

/* //BW: suggestion for non-orthogonality more than 85 if you cannot redo the mesh
    default           Gauss linear limited 0.333;
*/

/* //BW: suggestion for non-orthogonality between 70 and 85
    default           Gauss linear limited 0.5;
*/

/* //BW: suggestion for non-orthogonality between 60 and 70
    default           Gauss linear limited 0.777;
*/

/* //BW: suggestion for non-orthogonality between 40 and 60
    default           Gauss linear limited 1;
*/    	
     
}

